## 2026-06 Comic Library MVP

- Comic library is an optional module. The frontend hides comic navigation and comic import entry points until `comicLibraryEnabled=true`.
- Comic and movie domains are intentionally independent. Do not store comics in movie tables, do not model comics as `Movie`, and do not route comic behavior through `/api/library/movies` or `useLibraryService()`.
- Backend persistence uses separate SQLite tables and repositories: `comic_library_paths`, `comic_books`, `comic_pages`, `comic_tags`, `comic_book_tags`, `comic_reading_progress`, `comic_reading_preferences`, `comic_book_comments`, and `comic_cache_entries`.
- Backend routes: `POST /api/import/comics`; `GET/POST/PATCH/DELETE /api/library/comics/paths`; `POST /api/library/comics/scans` (optional `paths` body restricts scans to configured comic roots); `GET /api/library/comics/cache/status`; `POST /api/library/comics/cache/cleanup`; `GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/library/comics/{comicId}`; `POST /api/library/comics/books/{comicId}/reveal`; page image/thumbnail, progress, preference, and comment routes under `/api/library/comics/books/{comicId}/...`.
- Settings keys in `config/library-config.cfg`: `comicLibraryEnabled`, `autoComicLibraryWatch` (default `true`), `defaultComicImportLibraryPathId`, `comicReader` (`mode`, `fit`, `direction`), and `comicCache` (`maxBytes`, default 2147483648, negative means unlimited).
- Frontend routes: `/comics`, `/comics/:id`, and `/comics/:id/read/:page?` guarded by comic enabled state. Service boundary is `useComicLibraryService()` with independent web/mock adapters and `src/domain/comic` types.
- Archive support is `.zip` and `.cbz` only. Page images are `.jpg`, `.jpeg`, `.png`, `.webp`, and `.gif`. The first naturally sorted image is the cover, and natural sort respects directory hierarchy plus numeric filename order.
- Comic import copies archives into `defaultComicImportLibraryPathId`, never deletes source archives, never overwrites conflicts, and starts `scan.comics` after successful copy.
- Comic auto watch is independent from movie auto watch. When `libraryWatchEnabled` permits fsnotify, `comicLibraryEnabled=true`, and `autoComicLibraryWatch=true`, `backend/internal/comicwatch` watches `comic_library_paths` for `.zip` / `.cbz` create/write/rename events and queues App-owned `scan.comics` tasks with `metadata.trigger="fsnotify"`.
- Detail MVP fields are title, tags, rating, and favorite. Author/series can be represented as tags until explicit metadata fields exist.
- Reader supports page/scroll mode, contain/width fit, LTR/RTL keyboard navigation, persisted reading progress/preferences, and session-only current+previous/current+next stitching. The reader prefetches current±1 original `imageUrl` via hidden `Image()` and cancels on unmount.
- Comic cache is separate from movie assets/cache. Thumbnail writes respect `comicCache.maxBytes` (`< 0` unlimited) by evicting oldest `last_accessed_at` files+rows, skipping the key just written. Decode rejects sources over 32 MiB or 24M pixels with HTTP 422 and does not fall back to the original image. Cache cleanup deletes only comic cache entries/files inside the comic cache root and must not delete source `.zip` / `.cbz` archives.
- Comic and photo library walls use `DynamicScroller` with the same 4-rows-per-chunk model as the movie wall. Web adapters page lists in batches of 500 until `total`; entering `/comics` or `/photos` uses `ensureComicsLoaded` / `ensurePhotosLoaded` and skips reload when the list is already warm. Scan, import, and directory-watch completion still force `reload*FromApi`. List tags are loaded with one `IN (...)` query per page. `OpenPage` opens a ZIP entry directly without enumerating all pages.
- Task types: `scan.comics`, `import.comics`, and `comic.cache.cleanup`. Comic error codes use the `COMIC_*` prefix.
- MVP exclusions: metadata scraping, OCR, `.rar`, `.cbr`, `.7z`, persistent double-page layout, gamepad reader controls, and cross-device sync beyond local Web API SQLite state.

